{"word": "realtor", "source": "freedictionaryapi", "data": {"word": "realtor", "entries": [{"language": {"code": "en", "name": "English"}, "partOfSpeech": "noun", "pronunciations": [{"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈɹi(ə)l.təɹ/", "tags": ["US"]}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈɹi(ə)l.tɔɹ/", "tags": ["US"]}], "forms": [{"word": "realtors", "tags": ["plural"]}], "senses": [{"definition": "(Canada, US) A person or business that sells or leases out real estate, acting as an agent for the property owner.", "tags": ["Canada", "US"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "It was composed of an engineer, if I remember correctly, a town planner, a realtor, and occasionally an architect […]", "reference": "1919, Mr. Shannon, U.S. Housing Corporation. Hearings Before a Subcommittee, United States Senate:"}, {"text": "First place, we ought to insist that folks call us ‘realtors’ and not ‘real-estate men.’ Sounds more like a reg’lar profession.", "reference": "1922, Sinclair Lewis, Babbitt, New York, N.Y.: Harcourt, Brace and Company, →OCLC:"}, {"text": "Intrigued by the prospect of an additional commission, the realtor hurriedly assured me he foresaw no problem in obtaining the lease.", "reference": "1975, Jerzy Kosiński, Cockpit, Grove Press, published 1998, page 189:"}, {"text": "The terms agent, broker, and realtor are often used interchangeably.", "reference": "1997, Douglas A. Gray, Canadian home buying made easy, second edition, page 72:"}, {"text": "The realtor was like a carnivore, ready to spring. He was originally from New York and he seemed like the kind of guy who could smell a deal.", "reference": "2003, Gary Andrew Dresden, Confessions of a Gynecologist, iUniverse, page 111:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "bg", "name": "Bulgarian"}, "word": "посредник"}, {"language": {"code": "bg", "name": "Bulgarian"}, "word": "посредничка"}, {"language": {"code": "cmn", "name": "Chinese Mandarin"}, "word": "房地產經紀人 /房地产经纪人"}, {"language": {"code": "